window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Pirates, slavers, and deviants!</p> <p>Captain Sass Collier leads her motley crew across the treacherous rings of gas giant Pono, seeking a cure for the steady decline of Mahina Colony. Tantalizing clues point to Sagamore, Mahina’s sister moon.</p> <p>To get there, Sass needs to upgrade her decrepit skyship. Her crew of would-be heroes need to earn their space legs. And ex-cop Sass is probably the wrong person for the job.</p> <p>But no one else is willing to try.</p> <p>Only the deranged denizens of the rings can enable them to reach Sagamore. The social rejects in orbit prove as dangerous as the asteroids.</p> <p>But if Sass can’t figure out why the settlers are failing, her colony is doomed.</p> <p>Sass won't let that happen.</p> <p>If you love exciting civilian space adventure, with an ensemble cast of well-meaning misfits, you’ll love book 2 in Ginger Booth’s Thrive Space Colony Adventures. Suggested for fans of <i>Firefly </i>and Heinlein.</p>"; 
